# FATORI-V: Fault Injection Framework for RISC-V

Automated fault injection system for Ibex RISC-V cores on Xilinx FPGAs.

## System Overview

FATORI-V provides end-to-end automation from YAML configuration through
hardware generation, FPGA builds, benchmark execution with fault injection,
to results analysis.

Target: Ibex RISC-V core on Xilinx XCKU040 FPGAs
Integration: py2hwsw framework, Vivado 2020.2

## Directory Structure

benchmarks/     - Benchmark implementations (CoreMark, Embench, etc.)
config/         - Logging and system configuration
inputs/         - Static input files (YAML, TCL, hardware/software)
results/        - Per-run output and analysis
runs/           - Run configuration YAML files
scripts/        - Python control layer
tmp/            - Generated files and build intermediates

## Quick Start

1. Create run configuration: runs/my_run.yaml
2. Execute: python fatori-v.py my_run
3. Results in: results/my_run/

## Configuration

Run YAML files define:
- Target hardware (board, FPGA part)
- ISA extensions (RV32M, RV32C, etc.)
- Fault tolerance mechanisms
- Benchmarks to execute
- Fault injection parameters

See runs/example.yaml for complete template.

## Architecture Documentation

Each subsystem has a Readme in its directory:
- scripts/Readme - Python control layer overview
- inputs/Readme - Static input file specifications
- benchmarks/Readme - Benchmark integration

## Build Requirements

- Python 3.8+
- Xilinx Vivado 2020.2 or later
- RISC-V GNU toolchain
- py2hwsw framework

